Roll a Ball + Clock Projects

Both projects are located in the scenes folder
  Roll a Ball is labeled as MiniGame
  Clock is labeled as SampleScene

* Roll a Ball is a game designed around a player, where the objective is to collect all 12 cubes without getting caught by the enemy.
    The enemy is controlled using the NavMeshPro AI agent feature and is set to track the player.
    If the player is caught, the player object will be destroyed, and the screen will display a game over text.
    If the player successfully collects all twelve cubes, the enemy object will be destroyed and a text overlay saying "You Win!" will be displayed.
    The game also has a count feature on the screen so you know your score.

* The Clock is simply a dynamic game object that sets its time according to your computer's local time.
    The clock offers a second, minute, and hour hand ticking just like any analog clock.  
    There isn't much to the clock besides it displaying the time and incrementing it as well.
    The clock uses Quaternion.Euler() as its basis of movement.
